{{!-- "You are aboard X" strip, injected at the top of a character's own sheet while their token
      is riding a vehicle. The sheet is reachable from the sidebar with no token selected (and
      with no canvas at all), so this is the one surface a passenger can always get to.

      ⭐ When the aboard token is on a scene the viewer is NOT looking at, the strip names that
      scene and the control says it acts there. The control is deliberately still offered — it
      works, and it is the one way off a vehicle for someone whose token is elsewhere — but a
      Step Out button with no vehicle on screen has to say where it reaches. --}}
<div class="cp-aboard-banner{{#if remote}} cp-aboard-remote{{/if}}" data-token-id="{{tokenId}}" data-scene-id="{{sceneId}}">
    <i class="fas fa-van-shuttle cp-aboard-icon"></i>
    <span class="cp-aboard-text">
        {{#if remote}}{{CPLocal "Vehicle.AboardBannerElsewhere" vehicle=vehicleName scene=sceneName}}{{else}}{{CPLocal "Vehicle.AboardBanner" vehicle=vehicleName}}{{/if}}
    </span>
    <button type="button" class="cp-aboard-out"
            title="{{#if remote}}{{CPLocal 'Vehicle.StepOutTipElsewhere' scene=sceneName}}{{else}}{{CPLocal 'Vehicle.StepOutTip'}}{{/if}}">{{CPLocal "Vehicle.StepOut"}}</button>
</div>
